-- title:
--   Global sections of an affine fibre product are generated by the two factors
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a scheme (in a fixed universe) which is affine, let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings, and let $a : \operatorname{Spec} A \to S$ and $b : \operatorname{Spec} B \to S$ be morphisms of schemes. Form the fibre product $\operatorname{Spec} A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} B$ with its two projections `pullback.fst a b` and `pullback.snd a b`, and for each projection take the induced ring homomorphism on sections over the whole space, i.e. the component at the top open of the comorphism of sheaves: these are ring maps $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A, \mathcal{O}) \to \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} B, \mathcal{O})$ and $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} B, \mathcal{O}) \to \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} B, \mathcal{O})$. The assertion is that the subring of $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} B, \mathcal{O})$ generated by the union of the set-theoretic images of these two maps is the whole ring, i.e. equals $\top$. No flatness, finiteness or separatedness hypothesis is imposed, and the conclusion is about generation as a subring (not as an $A$- or $B$-algebra).
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic shadow of the description of a fibre product of affine schemes over an affine base as the spectrum of a tensor product: the global sections of $\operatorname{Spec} A \times_S \operatorname{Spec} B$ are generated by the pullbacks of sections from the two factors. It is used in the proof of [`AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_pullback_fst_preimage_inf_snd_preimage_and_closure_eq_top`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.isAffineOpen_pullback_fst_preimage_inf_snd_preimage_and_closure_eq_top), where the corresponding generation statement is needed for the intersection of the preimages of two affine opens inside a fibre product of arbitrary schemes.
